# Never bake into the image: secrets, local DBs, virtualenv, build artifacts.
# The build context is COPY'd into the image, so anything not excluded here
# ships inside every pushed layer (see docs/reviews/CODE_ANALYSIS_REPORT.md F-12).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.db
*.db-journal
# TLS material never ships inside an image layer (keys are secrets; the
# compose stack mounts the certs read-only at runtime instead).
*.key
*.crt
*.pem
infrastructure/nginx/certs/
data/
.venv/
venv/
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov/
docs/
tests/
ui/node_modules/
*.egg-info/
.venv*
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log

# BYOM: the image ships zero model weights — the operator mounts models/
# read-only at runtime (compose does this). Prevents an operator's local
# staging from leaking AGPL/research-restricted checkpoints into a layer.
models/staged/
